{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require council and private car parks to charge by the minute",
        "additional_details": "If you park for 35 minutes, you should pay for 35 minutes, not a full hour. If you pay for two hours but leave after one, you should get the unused hour refunded. We want council and private car parks to charge only for the time people actually park. This could help families save money and make visiting local shops and businesses more affordable. Fair parking means paying for what you use.",
        "background": "Introduce legislation requiring council and private parking operators to charge by the minute for the actual time parked, rather than rounding up to fixed blocks. Require pay-on-exit options or automatic refunds for unused prepaid time.",
